# Walking and turning at once -- can the game do it when asked?
#
# The shipped converter thresholds each stick axis at 100 of 127, so forward
# and turn could never both be requested from one round stick. In `dual` they
# can: left stick up walks, right stick turns. This holds each alone and both
# together, plus a diagonal push of the left stick and a walk back, with the
# camera's yaw and translation measured per frame.
#
#   scripts/09-replay.sh --decode --env PSPRECOMP_INPUT=dual \
#     --env PSPRECOMP_VIEW_LOG=reports/walk-turn.view \
#     --env PSPRECOMP_VIEW_LOG_WORLD=all \
#     --env PSPRECOMP_VIEW_LOG_POLLS=2130-2135,2210-2215,2290-2295,2370-2375,2450-2455,2530-2535 \
#     scenarios/walk-turn.pad
#   scripts/view-analyze.py reports/walk-turn.view --deltas

drain 500

@76     state circle 128 128   # t=3.080s
@78     state none 128 128   # t=3.160s
@176    state circle 128 128   # t=7.458s
@178    state none 128 128   # t=7.553s
@317    state circle 128 128   # t=13.327s
@318    state none 128 128   # t=13.379s
@331    state start 128 128   # t=14.028s
@333    state none 128 128   # t=14.135s
@359    state cross 128 128   # t=15.475s
@361    state none 128 128   # t=15.567s
@409    state circle 128 128   # t=18.664s
@411    state none 128 128   # t=18.800s
